[Music]  October is domestic violence awareness  month and safe house is here to talk  about why it is so critical to find help  and give help if you can joining us safe  house executive director Beth Flory I'm  so happy to have you here this is a  critical month we talk about domestic  violence people are aware that it's  happening and we're reporting on it all  too often why is it so important to  continue continue talking about it  so it's important to continue talking  about it one interesting data point that  I'd really like to share last year at  the end of the year agencies across  Nevada provided data about Services they  provided one of those numbers was 85 000  bed nights almost 85 000. so what that  means is that each night in Nevada last  year approximately  233 adults and children stayed in an  emergency shelter in a hotel or a motel  so that's 233 individuals that didn't go  home because they felt unsafe that  doesn't count the number of people who  maybe stayed with a family or friend or  stayed in their car or that student that  walked home to their dorm room after a  fight with their partner and it  definitely does not count all the people  who did not feel safe to leave their  abusive home I was going to say so many  don't so many are afraid to make that  call now you guys are based in Henderson  talk a little bit about what type of  service is that you provide so we  provide emergency shelter we have a  24-hour crisis hotline that victim  survivors can call anytime day or night  to get assistance we have Advocates that  can help with temporary protective  orders going to court it's so helpful to  have somebody sitting next to you when  you have to face your abusive partner  and we also have counseling services and  all of those services are free of charge  to victim survivors and their children  the first step  it is asking for that help getting that  help yes how what what are the warning  signs what are things that either you as  a victim might start to notice or you as  a friend might see what should we be  looking for so one big warning sign is  isolation abusive Partners have a  tendency to isolate you from your family  and friends we also see Financial abuse  being put down called names and then of  course that physical violence so any of  those signs where you start to feel  unsafe in your home is a good time to  call and ask for help and our hotline  operators they are very non-judgmental  they will listen to your story and they  will help you decide what you want to do  with your situation a lot of people  maybe are sitting at home and they're  thinking okay maybe I've seen this maybe  I haven't but I want to help because I  know that it's a problem what can what  can someone do you know that maybe  doesn't know a victim or a Survivor what  how can they help you so there's many  ways that you can and help we do have a  volunteer program where individuals go  through training on how to assist  victims of domestic violence in their  children and there's all all different  ways people can volunteer maybe if they  don't feel comfortable volunteering  directly with a victim Survivor they can  help with donations they can help at our  front desk any way possible we certainly  appreciate you being here on the show  and also you know being an advocate for  our people here in Nevada we know how  important it is I want to be able to  stop talking about this on the news and  I know you would probably love it if you  didn't have a job I absolutely would  love to put myself out of a job yes all  right Beth thank you so much for being  here this morning we appreciate it thank  you for inviting me  of course there are so many ways to  support safe house but there's one  tonight you can join in lots of fun a  Halloween Carnival from 6 to 8 30 at  Sunset Station the event for all ages  there's going to be games costume  contests even an ice cream bar

